{"id": "striviaqa0037", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 8.81, "n_chunks": 9, "n_concurrent": 9, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.5314, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "indianapolis 500 (accepted aliases: indianapolis 500 mile race, indy 500, indy 505, greatest spectecle in racing, greatest spectacle in racing, indy500, 500, international 500 mile sweepstakes race, international 500 mile sweepstakes, i)", "query": "In 2005, Dan Wheldon became the first British competitor to win what event in over 30 years?", "transcript": "In two thousand and five, Dan Weldon became the first British competitor to win what event in over thirty years?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The dragon watched silently as the baker worked, his tiny claws tapping against the stone wall. When the bread was ready, the baker placed a warm loaf into the dragon's waiting claws. The dragon took a bite and closed his eyes in bliss. From that day on, the village bakery always saved a special treat for the quiet green dragon who lived in the valley.", "answer_ms": 2394}
{"id": "striviaqa0040", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 12.17, "n_chunks": 13, "n_concurrent": 13, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.6689, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "new brighton (accepted aliases: new brighton disambiguation, new brighton)", "query": "Accrington Stanley’s biggest league win was 8-0 in 1934 when they beat which club from the Wirral who were members of the Football League from 1923 until 1951?", "transcript": "Aghrin Town, Stanley's biggest league win, was eight nil in nineteen thirty four when they beat which club from the Wirral, who were members of the Football League from nineteen twenty three until nineteen fifty one?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Aggerton, Stanley's biggest quiet valley beside a slow green river. Every morning, Stanley watched the village bakery as the baker knead the dough with steady hands. The dragon wanted to learn, so it practiced folding and stretching until 1951.", "answer_ms": 1678}
{"id": "striviaqa0043", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.75, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4897, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "lungs (accepted aliases: pulmonary gas exchange, pulmo sinister, pulmanary, inferior lobe, pulmonary surgical procedures, bird lung, lungs, lunged, superior lobe of left lung, alveolar sacs, avian lungs, pulmones, nonrespirat)", "query": "What in the human body are enclosed in the Pleura ?", "transcript": "What in the human body are enclosed in the pleura?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Lungs.", "answer_ms": 121}
{"id": "striviaqa0046", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 4.63, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2141, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "likes of us (accepted aliases: likes of us)", "query": "Andrew Lloyd Webber and Tim Rice first worked together on which musical?", "transcript": "Andrew Lloyd Webber and Tim Rice first worked together on which musical?", "mode": "local", "answer": "They first worked together on \"Jesus Christ Superstar\".", "answer_ms": 365}
{"id": "striviaqa0049", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.04, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2473, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "columbus (accepted aliases: columbus usa, columbus disambiguation, colombus, columbus)", "query": "What is the state capital of Ohio", "transcript": "What is the state capital of Ohio?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The capital of Ohio is Columbus.", "answer_ms": 242}
{"id": "striviaqa0052", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 34.2, "n_chunks": 35, "n_concurrent": 35, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.667, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "adventure (accepted aliases: adventurer, thrill seeking, adventure, adventurous, adventures, trill seeking, adventurers)", "query": "Which game that contained many D&D; features and references, including a computer controlled dungeon master, created in 1975 by Will Crowther on a DEC PDP-10 computer, the first widely used adventure game, was significantly expanded in 1976 by Don Woods, that inspired a group of students at MIT to write a game called Zork in the summer of 1977 for the PDP-10 minicomputer which became quite popular on the ARPANET?", "transcript": "Which game that contained many D&D features and references, including a computer controlled Dungeon Master, created in 1975 by Will Crowther on a DEC PDP-10 computer, the first widely used adventure game, was significantly expanded in 1976 by Don Woods, that inspired a group of students at MIT to write a game called Zork in the summer of 1977, for the PDP-10 minicomputer which became quite popular on the ARPANET?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time, in a quiet valley beside a slow green river, lived a small dragon. Every morning the dragon walked to the village bakery and watched the baker knead the dough with steady hands. The dragon wanted to learn, so it practiced folding and pressing the dough late into the evening, night after night, week after week. Slowly the loaves improved, first dense and burnt, then lighter and fluffier. The villagers began to look forward to the golden-brown bread each morning. The dragon greeted every traveler by name. In the winter the oven kept the whole square warm, and travelers came from far away just to taste the special dragon-baked bread. One summer day, a group of students at MIT visited the valley. They were inspired by the kindness of the dragon and decided to write a game called Zork. Years later, in 1977, for the PDP-10 minicomputer which became quite popular on the ARPANET, they created a computer-controlled Dungeon Master. That game, filled with adventure and mystery, spread across the world like wildfire. And somewhere deep in that digital dungeon, echoes of the small dragon's quiet valley could still be heard, reminding everyone that even the smallest acts of kindness can inspire greatness.", "answer_ms": 8983}
