{"id": "striviaqa0205", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 8.95, "n_chunks": 9, "n_concurrent": 9, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1292, "eot_read_ms": 33, "reference_answer": "big brother (accepted aliases: big brother disambiguation, big brother song, big brother film, bigbrother1, big brother, big bruvva, bigbrother)", "query": "What is a reality TV show in which a group of people live in a large house watched by cameras, first broadcast in the Netherlands in 1999?", "transcript": "What is a reality TV show in which a group of people live in a large house watched by cameras, first broadcast in the Netherlands in one thousand nine hundred and ninety nine?", "mode": "local", "answer": "A reality TV show is a type of television program in which participants are recorded in a real-life setting rather than being scripted or acted out. The situations they experience are genuine, though often arranged or influenced by producers to create compelling content for viewers. Common formats include competitions like \"Survivor\" or \"Big Brother,\" where contestants live together under specific rules and are observed continuously; talent-based shows such as \"America's Got Talent\"; or lifestyle-based programs like \"Keeping Up with the Kardashians,\" where people document their everyday lives. Reality TV became popular in the late 1990s and early 2000s, offering audiences a glimpse into the personal and competitive lives of others, often with a focus on drama, challenges, or unique personalities.", "answer_ms": 5382}
{"id": "striviaqa0208", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 12.32, "n_chunks": 13, "n_concurrent": 13, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.7788, "eot_read_ms": 32, "reference_answer": "david hilbert (accepted aliases: hilbertian, david hilbert, hilbert david, david hillbert, gordan s problem, hilbert)", "query": "Who presented a list of 23 problems in mathematics at a conference of the International Congress of Mathematicians on 8 August 1900 in the Sorbonne, of which only 10 have resolutions which are fully accepted?", "transcript": "Who presented a list of twenty three problems in mathematics at a conference of the International Congress of Mathematicians on the eighth of August one thousand nine hundred in the Sorbonne, of which only ten have resolutions which are fully accepted?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time a small dragon lived in a quiet valley beside a slow green river. Every morning the dragon walked to the village bakery and watched the baker knead the dough with steady hands. The resolutions which are fully accepted by the community include continued support for the local school program, expansion of the community garden, and funding for the annual summer festival.", "answer_ms": 2424}
